# The harnesses whose binaries were never listed. csstest and fbtext have been
# built by ./build.sh since they were written and have shown up as untracked
# ever since; pngtest is new. A build output that is merely UNLISTED rather
# than ignored is one `git add -A` away from being committed, which is how
# _genefi.c got into this repo in the first place.
kernel/hosttest/csstest
kernel/hosttest/fbtext
kernel/hosttest/pngtest
kernel/hosttest/csstest_san
kernel/hosttest/pngtest_san
kernel/hosttest/browsertest_san
kernel/hosttest/arenatest
kernel/hosttest/settingstest
kernel/hosttest/systest
# parsestat is the measuring instrument for the parser caps (browser-storage-run.md).
# Listed the same day its .c was written, because four ELF binaries in this
# directory ARE tracked and dirty ~5 MB on every gate run - and each of them got
# there by being merely unlisted at the moment somebody ran `git add -A`.
kernel/hosttest/parsestat
kernel/hosttest/rtctest
kernel/hosttest/fstest
kernel/hosttest/exectest
kernel/hosttest/libctest
kernel/hosttest/toasttest
kernel/hosttest/tritest
kernel/hosttest/jstest
kernel/hosttest/x509test
kernel/hosttest/ecdsatest
kernel/hosttest/tlstest
kernel/hosttest/cryptotest
kernel/hosttest/tlscryptotest
kernel/hosttest/jmptest
