kernel/hosttest/memtypetest
kernel/hosttest/msctest
# NOT *.ppm here: kernel/.gitignore:25 already says hosttest/*.ppm, and
# browsershot.ppm and wmshot.ppm are TRACKED - so that rule does nothing for
# them (a tracked file is never ignored) while looking like it does. Adding a
# second copy of a rule that is already inert would make it harder to find,
# not easier. Both are ~5 MB and are rewritten by every gate run, so every
# visual gate produces a multi-megabyte diff. Untracking them is a call for
# whoever owns those goldens.

# build outputs - regenerable, and large. Build them with:
#   kernel/build.sh      kernel.elf        (BIOS multiboot)
#   kernel/mkdisk.sh     zlOS.img          (our own bootloader)
#   kernel/mkiso.sh      zlOS.iso          (hybrid BIOS/UEFI)
#   kernel/buildefi.sh   BOOTX64.EFI       (stage-0 UEFI witness)
#                        ZLOS.EFI          (native UEFI kernel)
#   kernel/mkusb.sh      zlOS-usb.img      (bootable USB image)
kernel/*.elf
kernel/*.img
kernel/*.iso
kernel/BOOTX64.EFI
kernel/ZLOS.EFI
kernel/BOOTX64.lib
kernel/_gen*.c
kernel/hosttest/intel_probe
kernel/hosttest/htmltest
kernel/hosttest/browsershot
